.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume-setup
writes the files
.BR yumed (8)
and
.BR yume (1)
run from: a server directory with its configuration, credentials and
cover site, client bundles for it, and an operator's signed cluster
list.
It starts neither program and opens no network connection, except that
.B cluster-sign
resolves a node's host when the node has no address.
.PP
Keys, certificates and signatures come from the OpenSSL release YUME is
built with, through the same readers
.B yume
and
.B yumed
use, so setup needs no
.B openssl
command or other runtime.
Every key is read back by those readers before setup writes it.
.PP
Secret files are created owner-only, exclusively and without following a
symlink.
A new kit, bundle or operator directory is written under a private
staging name beside its target and renamed into place without replacing
anything, so a failed command leaves no partial directory.
Commands that change an existing server or cluster write each replaced
file beside it and rename it over the old one.
Each replacement is atomic, but a command that touches several files is
not one filesystem transaction.
Before publication, failed cluster edits and
.B add-client
remove their newly created files even if rollback bookkeeping runs out
of memory.
Once a replacement publishes references to those files, a later failure
preserves them and reports the partial publication.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B tune
Apply one preset or one expert tuning limit to an existing client
configuration.
Exactly one of
.B --preset
and
.B --set
is required.
The complete original and resulting documents must pass the schema-1
parser.
Server documents, symlinks, special files, duplicate keys and invalid
values are refused before writing.
Other configuration members are preserved.
The result replaces the file atomically with mode 0600 and retains its
owner when run by root.
A failed write leaves the original intact and removes staging files.
A failure flushing the parent directory after replacement reports an
error, but the new configuration is already visible.
Serialize edits to this file.
No credentials are opened and no session is restarted.
Restart the client separately to use the change; the server may cap the
chosen epoch.
.TP
.B init
Create a new kit directory holding
.B server/
and a first client bundle in
.BR client/ .
The server gets a composite Ed25519 and ML-DSA-87 identity, an
ML-KEM-1024 key, a P-256 TLS certificate from a one-off CA whose key is
never written, the deployment's admission key, an authorized-keys store
with the client, an empty admin-keys store and a static cover site.
The client gets its own identity, its access PSK and the server's public
material.
.TP
.B add-client
Issue another client bundle for an existing server directory.
The client is added to the server's authorized-keys store with the kit's
.B tcp
and
.B udp
services, and the store is replaced last.
A failure while flushing a directory after that replacement returns exit
status 3.
The store and the files it names remain visible, but directory
durability was not confirmed.
Validate the server tree before reloading it.
Files added to the server tree keep the store's owner.
A running daemon accepts the client once it reloads (SIGHUP).
.TP
.B remove-client
Take a client out of a server's authorized-keys store, then delete its
public key and access PSK.
The last client cannot be removed, because the daemon requires one.
A running daemon ends the client's sessions when it reloads.
.TP
.B cluster-init
Create an operator directory with a new composite operator key, the key
network tags are made under and an empty cluster record.
Keep it off the servers.
.TP
.B cluster-add
Enter a server directory into a cluster.
The server's TLS certificate must name
.BR --host .
For every node already in the cluster, a fresh PSK for each direction
goes into both nodes' peer stores with the other node's admission key,
and the new server gets the operator's public key and a
.B cluster
section in its
.BR yumed.json .
The cluster record is replaced last.
A failure after the first replacement returns exit status 3 and keeps
every file already referenced.
.TP
.B cluster-remove
Take a node out of a cluster.
Every other node forgets it, and the removed node loses its cluster
section and its
.B credentials/cluster
directory, so it runs alone after a restart.
Its saved serial is removed only through a relative path inside its
server directory, without parent traversal or symlinked directories.
Sign a new list afterwards.
.TP
.B cluster-sign
Sign the next cluster list and routes view and copy them to every node.
The serial goes up by one, and both expire after
.BR --days .
The routes view names each node, its identity, its exit mark and its
network tag, and no address.
Both are checked with the readers the nodes use before anything is
written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--host " host
The DNS name or IP literal the server's TLS certificate names, which
clients authenticate.
Required by
.BR init ,
.B add-client
and
.BR cluster-add .
.TP
.BI "--output " directory
The new directory
.BR init ,
.B add-client
or
.B cluster-init
writes.
Its parent must be an existing directory, and nothing may exist at the
path.
.TP
.BI "--port " port
The port
.B init
writes into both configurations, from 1 to 65535.
.TP
.BI "--client-name " name
The client's name in the authorized-keys store: 1 to 63 letters, digits,
.BR . ,
.B _
or
.BR - ,
beginning and ending with a letter or digit.
.B init
uses
.B client1
without it, and
.B add-client
and
.B remove-client
require it.
.TP
.BI "--max-sessions " count
How many sessions the client may hold at once, from 1 to 1024.
A newer session replaces the oldest.
Without it the daemon sets no per-client bound.
.TP
.BI "--weight " weight
The client's share of the server's egress rate against other busy
clients, from 0.1 to 100.
.TP
.BI "--max-egress-mbps " rate
For
.BR init :
the server's stream egress rate in Mbit/s, from 1 to 1000000, which
clients share by weight.
Unlimited when omitted.
.TP
.BI "--preset " preset
For
.BR init :
the tuning preset both configurations take.
For
.BR tune :
the preset applied to the client.
Each trades far-path speed against how much data one key protects and
how close the carrier stays to browser traffic.
.B stealth
is the default.
A client from
.B add-client
takes its server's tuning.
.TP
.BI "--config " file
For
.BR tune :
an existing schema-1 client configuration, at most 1 MiB.
.TP
.BI "--set " key=JSON
For
.BR tune :
one of
.BR max_queued_bytes ,
.BR max_epoch_bytes ,
.B credit_returns_per_window
or
.BR idle_epoch_rotation ,
followed by
.B =
and a JSON number or boolean.
Use bytes for budgets and epochs, and
.B true
or
.B false
for idle rotation.
The configuration reference owns the bounds.
This writes the file; it is not a per-run security override.
.TP
.BI "--server " directory
A server directory in the layout
.B init
writes, holding
.B yumed.json
and its credentials.
.TP
.B --circuits
For
.BR add-client :
grant the client
.B yume.circuit
and give its bundle a
.B circuits
section of three hops, with this server as the entry, and the kit's
copies of the operator key and routes view.
The server must belong to a signed cluster.
Circuits carry TCP only, so the bundle's SOCKS5 adapter refuses UDP.
.TP
.BI "--cluster " directory
The operator directory
.B cluster-init
created, which holds the operator key and the cluster record.
Required by every cluster action.
.TP
.BI "--name " name
The node's name in the cluster list, by the same rule as a client name.
.TP
.BI "--address " address
For
.BR cluster-add :
an IP literal other nodes dial instead of resolving
.BR --host .
TLS still authenticates the host.
It also gives the node's network tag; without it
.B cluster-sign
resolves the host.
.TP
.B --exit
For
.BR cluster-add :
the node carries circuits' streams to destinations through its one
.B direct_tcp
adapter and that adapter's destination policy.
.TP
.BI "--days " days
For
.BR cluster-sign :
how long the list and routes view stay valid, from 1 to 366 days.
A node whose list has expired closes its links.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print the actions and options and exit.
.PP
An option may also be written as
.BR --option=value .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
when the action fails,
.B 2
for a usage error, and
.B 3
when files were published but the change is incomplete: a directory
flush failed after a replacement, or a later replacement of the same
command failed.
Validate the affected tree before a daemon reloads it.
A failure prints one line beginning
.B yume-setup:
and names no secret.
.SH FILES
A kit from
.B init
holds
.BR manifest.json ,
.B server/yumed.json
with
.BR server/credentials/ ,
.BR server/cover-site/ ,
.B server/services/
and
.BR server/start-server ,
and
.B client/yume.json
with
.BR client/credentials/ ,
.B client/adapters/
and
.BR client/start-client .
.B docs/OPERATIONS.md
describes deploying them and
.B docs/protocol/CLUSTER_1.md
the cluster files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
yume-setup init --host vpn.example.net --output "$PWD/yume-kit"
yume-setup add-client --server yume-kit/server --host vpn.example.net \e
  --output "$PWD/tablet" --client-name tablet --max-sessions 2
yume-setup remove-client --server yume-kit/server --client-name tablet
yume-setup tune --config yume-kit/client/yume.json --preset stealth-16
yume-setup tune --config yume-kit/client/yume.json --set max_epoch_bytes=2097152
.fi
